From egsmith-fWAZDB8bsKe+fmr0zi+kZQ at public.gmane.org  Fri Mar 29 23:57:22 2013
From: egsmith-fWAZDB8bsKe+fmr0zi+kZQ at public.gmane.org (Smith, Evann)
Date: Fri, 29 Mar 2013 23:57:22 +0000
Subject: Re: sim() problems with ordered logit: incorrect dimensions
In-Reply-To: <2AD59FAD-A824-4562-B2F3-27212D89D7F9@fas.harvard.edu>
References: <2AD59FAD-A824-4562-B2F3-27212D89D7F9@fas.harvard.edu>
Message-ID: <B2441A3D93C47B469CC60890F7666A6A04F629@HARVANDMBX01.fasmail.priv>

In case anyone is wondering, I figured out my problems.

1) I needed to set my dependent variable as a factor outside the zelig call.
2) It didn't like that I had missing data (which produced NAs in the setx values). Listwise deletion prior to running the model solved that problem.

Cheers,
Evann

